The World��s Biggest Bookstore in downtown Toronto will close forever on March 30 — one week later than originally announced, in apparent response to the popularity of its closing sale.
But the snapshots of the place shared on social media lead one to wonder whether there will be much left by the time the 33-year-old red-headed stepchild of the Indigo chain closes its doors.
Perhaps the final hours of business will provide an opportunity to see which books are the least popular in Canada after weeks of being sold for at least half of their cover prices: An Astronaut��s Guide to Life on Earth by Chris Hadfield has remained particularly abundant based on comments from visitors.
