9 Gallery: Cleveland Indians lose to Tampa Bay Rays, 10-3
CLEVELAND, Ohio — While the runs mounted, Justin Masterson's mind wandered. He thought about throwing left-handed. He thought about copying Joe Smith's submarine style of pitching. He thought about being a nice guy.
In the end, all that mattered was that Tampa Bay beat the Indians, 10-3, Friday night at Progressive Field.
Masterson's first pitch of the game to Desmond Jennings landed in center field for a single. His second pitch bounced past catcher Carlos Santana for the first of two wild pitches. A pattern was developing.
