"My big brother was B.I.G.'s brother" - Kanye West, "Big Brother"
Earlier today, Kanye West announced that he was hitting the road with a new blockbuster tour featuring Kendrick Lamar across North America. About an hour later, Kanye's big brother, Jay Z, stole a little bit of his young brother's shine with the announcement that he was extending the tour dates of his Magna Carter World Tour into North America.
This is not the first time that both Rocafella alumni have tried to shine block one another. Despite their frequent collaborations and longstanding friendship, both members of The Throne have been engaged in a game of one-upmanship for years now. XXL has compiled a timeline of the important events in which the duo has attempted to out-do one another.
The Timeline
June 25, 1996 - Jay Z releases Reasonable Doubt eight years before Kanye releases College Dropout. A clear potshot at a teenaged Kanye's inability to have a successful rap career until almost a decade later.
1997 - 2003 - Jay Z releases 10 more albums before Kanye. Hov is clearly rubbing it in.
November 14, 2003 - Jay retires just to prove his point to Kanye.
February 10, 2004 - Kanye finally releases his debut album, The College Dropout. On the song, "Last Call," Kanye documents Jay Z dismissive behavior towards his burgeoning rap career. Meanwhile during the introduction, an annoyed Jay Z tells Kanye "Yo, fuck you, Kanye first and foremost for making me do this shit."
July 2005 - Jay Z jumps on the remix of Kanye's "Diamonds Of Sierra Leone" and ruins Kanye's Christmas. Years later, Kanye would take to time complain about about it on "Big Brother."
November 21, 2005 - Kanye tells Jay Z that he is doing a song with Coldplay and soon after, Jay Z releases "Beach Chair" his song produced by Chris Martin Of Coldplay.
